#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand snap install modes, including classic, devmode, jailmode, and "
"dangerous options for testing, troubleshooting, and development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:8
msgid "Install modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:10
msgid ""
"A snap can be installed with the following optional arguments, typically "
"used to help test a snap under development, troubleshoot interface issues, "
"or debug application crashes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:12
msgid ""
"In addition to the modes described below, `--transaction` can be used to "
"install a set of snaps as a single transaction. See {ref}`Transactional "
"updates <explanation-how-snaps-work-transactional-updates>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:14
msgid "Classic confinement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:16
msgid ""
"The `--classic` argument is required for snaps that need access to more "
"system resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:18
msgid ""
"By default, a snap will attempt to install with _strict confinement_. Strict "
"confinement is used by the majority of snaps, enabling them to run their "
"applications and services in complete isolation with a minimal access level "
"that’s always deemed safe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:20
msgid ""
"Certain snaps, however, require unfettered access to the system, and these "
"are packaged as _classic snaps_. Installing a snap that requires classic "
"access will prompt the user to use the additional `--classic` argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:22
msgid "sudo snap install snapcraft --classic\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:26
msgid ""
"Only _classic_ snaps can be installed with the `--classic` argument. "
"However, while the argument is silently accepted when installing a strict "
"snap, it won't make any difference to its confinement. The snap will still "
"be strictly confined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:28
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Snap confinement <explanation-security-snap-confinement>` for more "
"details on confinement levels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:31
msgid "Dangerous mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:33
msgid ""
"The `--dangerous` argument will install a local snap without validating or "
"checking its assertions or signatures. These signatures are used to link a "
"snap to its publisher and store, and to ensure that a snap remains unchanged "
"during delivery and storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:35
msgid ""
"This option is useful when testing snaps shared through a trusted channel, "
"and for testing snaps built locally, before eventually being published to "
"the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:37
msgid ""
"The `snap refresh --amend` command can be used to replace a locally "
"installed snap with an identically named snap on the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:39
msgid "Developer mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:41
msgid ""
"The `--devmode` argument grants the snap **full access to system resources** "
"but will also report each access when no appropriate interface has been "
"specified. This report is sent to the system log. This mode is intended to "
"help snap developers identify the {ref}`interfaces <explanation-interfaces-"
"all-about-interfaces>` an application needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:43
msgid ""
"This feature allows developers to iterate over their snap, selectively "
"adding interfaces to their application before switching to _strict mode_ "
"after all necessary interfaces have been specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:45
msgid ""
"The validity of a snap's signed assertions will also be checked, linking a "
"snap to its developer and store, but the installation will progress even "
"when the validity cannot be verified. In this case, the _devmode_ snap is "
"additionally equivalent to being installed with `--dangerous`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:47
msgid ""
"A strictly confined snap running in _devmode_ will generate log and AppArmor "
"profile output associated with the snap, helping snap developers and testers "
"understand access issues and other confinement problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:49
msgid ""
"The _devmode_ argument is also a requirement  if a snap has been built and "
"published with `confinement: devmode` in its snapcraft.yaml. These snaps are "
"built for testing and cannot be released to their respective stable channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:51
msgid ""
"Additionally, snaps running in development mode will not be updated. This is "
"because it's assumed the snap developer wishes to test, and continue "
"testing, a specific release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:53
msgid "Jail mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:55
msgid ""
"The `--jailmode` argument will force the snap to install with strict "
"confinement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:57
msgid ""
"Only non-classic snaps can be placed in jail mode. This can be useful when "
"testing how a snap published with developer mode will behave when strictly "
"confined, and is usually a precursor to a snap being published as confined "
"and stable after a period of testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:59
msgid "Check snap install mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:61
msgid ""
"The `snap list` command will include the install mode status in the _Notes_ "
"column for each respective snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/snap-development/install-modes.md:63
msgid ""
"Name        Version            Rev    Tracking        Publisher     Notes\n"
"liquidctl   1.7.1-11-g6295354  1      latest/stable   morrisong     devmode\n"
"snapcraft   5.0                6751   latest/stable   canonical✓    classic\n"
msgstr ""
